  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "# Changelog\n\n## 0.2.10\n\n- Alinha a família de pacotes à integração OpenID Connect e à seleção configurável de endpoints do ApiExplorer, preservando os contratos existentes deste pacote.\n\n## 0.2.9\n\n- Alinha as dependências com a família 0.2.9, preservando o opt-in próprio do middleware e o runtime HTTP.\n\n## 0.2.8\n\n- Alinha o middleware e o runtime HTTP compartilhado com a família 0.2.8, incluindo a entrega offline ainda não publicada.\n\n## 0.2.7\n\n- Compartilha a escrita das respostas estáticas e geradas com o runtime HTTP offline.\n- Expõe o matching com caminhos estáticos e de contratos separados, preservando a semântica de escape.\n- Preserva Content-Length em HEAD sem escrever o corpo de respostas estáticas.\n\n## 0.2.6\n\n- Align the package version with the dependency maintenance release; middleware behavior is unchanged.\n\n## 0.2.5\n\n- Render Contract rules from their published documents through Gapfy.Echo.Contracts instead of the example body.\n- Keep missing or invalid Contract rules selectable and return the hosted 502 problem response without calling the next middleware.\n- Apply the hosted Contract header and active-content policy; preserve Static behavior and existing delay options.\n\n## Service change on 2026-09-14\n\n- Echo moved the rule feed to the paid plans. This was a service change, not a package release: an already installed 0.2.3 server can stop obtaining rules on Free without this package changing.\n- With no rules loaded, requests continue through the application pipeline and the failed refresh is logged. Rules already in memory or on disk remain active until the package is disarmed or its cache is cleared.\n\n## 0.2.3\n\n- Align the package version with the readable contract JSON release; embedded middleware behavior is unchanged.\n\n## 0.2.2\n\n- Validate route patterns with the runtime matcher when compiling a rule set and name rejected patterns in warnings.\n- Preserve the embedded host's configurable response header policy; hosted authoring uses the public host allowlist.\n- Correct public documentation and product links.\n- Include NuGet release notes and symbols in the coordinated Echo package release.\n\n## 0.2.0\n\n- Read the hierarchical rule feed shared with the mock client package.\n- Keep implemented endpoints in control and pass unmatched requests to the next middleware.\n\n## 0.1.1\n\n- Resolve rooted request paths consistently on every OS instead of parsing them as file URIs on Linux.\n\n## 0.1.0\n\n- Introduce ASP.NET Core middleware that serves Echo mock rules for unimplemented endpoints.\n- Pass unmatched requests through and fetch rule snapshots without blocking application startup.\n- Require explicit opt-in before arming in Production.",
